Z||000000||Hock||05-05-2000||04:23 AM||||OGRE HAS SOME GOOD INFO THERE. BUT I FOUND ONE PROBLEM.<BR>I WENT TO THE 4 CYLINDER SECTION AND HE LIST THAT THE 85 2.5L HAD FLAT TAPPET CAM. THAT IS WRONG. GM CHANGED FROM FLAT TAPPET TO ROLLER TAPPET FOR THE 85 MODEL YEAR.<BR>SO IF ITS POSSIBLE TRY TO GET THAT CHANGED SO NOBODY GETS LEAD THE WRONG DIRECTION WHEN DEALING WITH THESE ENGINES||||reg||3
Z||000001||Standard||05-05-2000||04:45 AM||||I believe it was a rolling change in 85, and wasn't official(sp) until 86.  GM does that alot.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||05-05-2000||09:45 AM||||Officially 85 is flat from everything I can find. I didn't see any mention of it at all untill 86. Are you sure yours is the original motor? Allot of 84-85 4 cyls got the motors dealer replaced, because of that it's posible that even some 84's have the roller cams.<P>I don't know which cave you where in..... the whole thing is being redug and enlarged. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-05-2000).]||||reg||1
